implementationPlan.note:
sh implementation: task_branch_landed, worktree_stop and provision_worktree after git_top(), the MOE_WT_* reset next to MOE_TOP="", and the worker-only call site directly above the Pre-flight landing block. bash -n OK. The file's codes are exactly the 7 MOE_WORKTREE_/MOE_CONTROL_ codes. Saved with the rename-safe Edit tool.

Held-out suite results:
- Linux bash: 12/12 ok; path-long is n/a off win32.
- Windows Git Bash via node.exe: 13/13 ok, path-long included. Log: C:\Users\Yaron\AppData\Local\Temp\c2046.cNut5a\gitbash.log.

Extra scratch probes (/mnt/d/moe-scratch/c20464ff/extra/extra.cjs, not delivered): 11/11 ok. They cover the gaps WT-04T noted:
- an ancestor sha on a foreign ref passes;
- own-ref, target-ref and non-checkpoint rows are ignored;
- an unknown sha refuses;
- blank, null and @{-1} targets refuse;
- .moe as a file or as a dangling link refuses;
- a Windows-spelled gitdir is repaired, then reused with its dirt intact;
- W registered on another branch refuses;
- a read-tree failure on a re-added W with commits keeps W, and the next session finishes it (reused).

Deviations, measured on git 2.43:
(1) CLAIM_RESULT/PREFLIGHT_CONTEXT reach python on stdin, separated by \x1e, not through env vars. Linux caps a single env string at 128 KiB, and get_context replies reach about 75 KB.
(2) The CREATE_FAILED detail carries the LAST line of git's output, not the first. The first line is 'Preparing worktree (new branch ...)'.
(3) An unregistered W that already exists refuses with CREATE_FAILED before `worktree add`. Measured: `worktree add -b` onto an existing directory fails but still creates the branch.
(4) printf instead of echo -e for the [ERROR], [WARN] and [worktree] lines, so backslashes in paths are never interpreted. The output is identical.
(5) git ls-files captures stdout only, so a warning on stderr can't hide an empty index.

sparse-checkout runs with MSYS2_ARG_CONV_EXCL='*', per WT-04T comment c9765599.

comments.content:
Contract correction from the WT-S revision after QA reject 1. Where this comment and the row's description differ, the revised docs/plans/2026-10-30-per-task-worktrees.md and this comment win. Section numbers are unchanged. Plan against revised §1.4 and §1.6:
1. The `.moe/` guard now FAILS CLOSED. This replaces "Warn MOE_WORKTREE_MOE_PRESENT if W/.moe exists", which rail 3 forbids. If `W/.moe` exists after create or reuse (a link counts):
   - print MOE_WORKTREE_MOE_PRESENT;
   - launch no CLI;
   - delete nothing and commit nothing, including no §3.3 recovery checkpoint;
   - call report_blocked with the code.
   Required negative case in postflight.{sh,ps1}: pre-create `W/.moe/x`, then assert that no CLI launched, `W/.moe/x` is still there, moe/task/<id> has no new commit, and report_blocked carried the code.
2. Add `--no-track` to `git worktree add … -b moe/task/<taskId>`.
3. Cutting W from the local target is still right for this slice. WT-09 switches the remote-mode base to refs/remotes/origin/<target> after its fetch (§1.2).
Everything else in the row is unchanged.
